{
  "title": "Split global web styles by page and component owner",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/App.css is roughly 3,900 lines and contains \
layout, navigation, shared controls, and nearly every page and component style \
in one global sheet. This increases selector-collision risk and makes \
otherwise narrow UI changes require scanning an unrelated monolith.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- Divide App.css into a small global/layout layer plus page- or \
component-owned styles using the project's existing CSS approach.\n\
- Preserve the current cascade deliberately; do not rename selectors or change \
specificity unless required to keep behavior identical.\n\
- Keep palette and shared design tokens centralized rather than duplicating \
them.\n\
- Make the move in reviewable groups and verify cookbook, recipe view/form, \
shopping list, meal plan, tags, modals, navigation, and responsive breakpoints \
with existing UI tests and screenshots.\n\
- Keep this mechanical: no visual refresh, CSS framework, CSS-in-JS \
dependency, or new design system.\n\
\n\
This is web-only cleanup and should be independent from the CookbookPage \
component split.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
